Sat-Sun, July 7-8. Plus halfday tour & social on the 6th.

8 full talks, 4 language specific minitalks, 2 discussions, 1
workshop, and of course the live unveiling of the first LCC conlang
relay (email David Peterson if you want to participate).

Schedule will be made public soon.

So: hey you! Yes, you! You know you want to be there amidst all the
conlanging awesomeness. Book your flight now and register at
http://lcc.questionform.com/public/LCC2-Timing .

If you want to give a minitalk (15 minutes) about YOUR language,
contact me ASAP - there's still *some* room but not much!

We are also starting to organize LCC3. It is too early to say for
certain, but we're expecting it to take place at the University of
Rochester in April 2008, under the direction of Sally Caves as
conference chair, and have a somewhat artistic / literary theme. If
you want to participate, please contact either of us.

